# The repository root is the build context of the server image, the computer image and the
# restore drill's image. A local `docker build -f images/<name>/Dockerfile .` reads that
# Dockerfile's own `Dockerfile.dockerignore` instead of this file. Wrangler passes the Dockerfile
# on stdin (`docker build -f -`), so BuildKit cannot find those and reads this file: it is their
# union, plus the drill's sources, with the same exclusions. Without it, a local `__pycache__`
# would reach the server image, and a checkout's state would change the image's digest, which
# the server's watchdog restarts the server for (scripts/test/dockerignore.test.ts).
*
# The server image (images/server/Dockerfile.dockerignore).
!images/server/cfo_server/
!images/server/services/
!python/cloudflare_omnigent/
!images/server/tests/
!images/server/Dockerfile
!contracts/schema/
# The computer image (images/computer/Dockerfile.dockerignore).
!images/computer/
!contracts/fixtures/
!contracts/vectors/
!python/tests/computer/
!worker/test/fixtures/workspace-commands.json
# Both images: the trust check and pip pin they bind-mount, and the computer's test stage.
!images/trust/
# The restore drill (scripts/restore-drill/staging/Dockerfile, which has no file of its own).
!scripts/restore-drill/cfo_drill/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/.hypothesis/
